spoint runtime client-side Draco is now PURE-JS (no WASM). streaming-gltf 1.0.11 vendors examples/local-progressive/draco-loader.js (mrdoob draco.js, ~110KB) consumed by model-pool.js + lod-worker.js (LOD workers fetch it same-origin, rewrite the bare 'three' import to esm.sh, import via blob URL). spoint integration: package.json dep ^1.0.11 (npm install pulls it into node_modules; server serves /node_modules statically; gh-pages copies the whole streaming-gltf pkg dir so draco-loader.js rides along). CLIENT-WIDE removal: client/core/SceneSetup.js createLoaders replaced three's WASM DRACOLoader (setDecoderPath('/draco/')+setWorkerLimit(4)+preload) with import { DRACOLoader } from 'streaming-gltf/draco-loader' (importmap alias in client/index.html -> node_modules path; setDecoderPath is a no-op). Deleted the dead ~2MB client/draco/ WASM assets + their gh-pages cp line. NO perf regression: player avatar (cleetus.vrm) + anim-lib.glb are NOT draco-compressed (verified, no extensions), so the JS decoder only ever runs on baked map models that already used the pool's JS loader; net win = no /draco/*.wasm fetch + no 4 decoder worker threads. Server/dev-time WASM draco kept (src/physics/DracoDecompressor.js draco3dgltf for collider extraction; src/static/GLBDraco.js + scripts/glb-processor.js draco3d/@gltf-transform for bake-time encoding) - Node-only, not client fetches, matching streaming-gltf's decode-JS / encode-WASM split. Browser-witnessed: 0 /draco/*.wasm fetches, draco-loader.js used 7x, player VRM (53 bones) + sillos map decode 0 errors. Commits ba1ed4eb (integration) + perf commit. Related [[modelpool-integration]] [[vrm-multidriver-player-routing]].